// Live-test fix (A): a creature on a version without custom mob models (no assets.creature) is built honestly.
const CREATURE_FALLBACK = " If the request describes a creature or mob: this version has no custom mob models or skins, so build it on a fitting vanilla base mob (Attribute.SCALE for its size), give it custom sounds for its voice where sounds are allowed, and a custom-textured item for anything it throws or drops where textures are allowed (a thrown rock: a Snowball with setItem(<the custom rock item>)); say in modbuilder.json limitations that its body keeps the vanilla mob's look.";
function assetsBlock(assets) {
