- synth presets and their params (all optional, clamped to the range): ${presetDocs}.
- processing (per variant, optional): {"lowpass": Hz 200-20000, "highpass": Hz 20-5000, "reverb": 0-1, "echo": {"delay": ms 20-1000, "feedback": 0-0.7, "mix": 0-1}}. Nxeon trims silence, sets the loudness for the role and limits peaks itself; do not do that with gain.
${library ? `- Sound library: ${"sound-library/catalog.txt"} in the working directory lists the Nxeon library: one line per sound with its id (the id names the sound), its duration class (stinger < 0.5 s, short < 2 s, medium < 6 s, long) and its use cases (weapon_fire, weapon_reload, mob_hurt, mob_death, ability_cast, ui_notification, ...), grouped by category (Weapons, Creatures & Voices, Impacts & Destruction, Movement, Magic & Energy, ...). Read it ONCE (it is read-only and not part of the plugin), then use ids exactly as listed: {"source": "lib:<id>"}. A library sound may never ship unchanged: change its pitch, layer it with another sound or a synth, or add lowpass/highpass/reverb/echo. 
